# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# For the committed static API that is not cosmetic — it breaks two things.
#
#  1. The pipeline writes LF (`Path.write_bytes`). With autocrlf the checked-out
#     file has CRLF, so a rebuild on UNCHANGED data would report all ~980 files
#     as modified. The determinism the build works so hard for would be invisible
#     and every diff would be noise.
#  2. Time series are stored one observation per line so a daily refresh is a
#     few KB of git delta. Line-ending churn would rewrite every line of every
#     file, which is the exact cost the line structure exists to avoid.
#
# So the data tree is pinned to LF. Nothing reads these files as text on
# Windows; they are served over HTTP and parsed as JSON.
frontend/public/api/** text eol=lf

# Source too, for the same "the file on disk is what got committed" reason.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.xlsx binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
